  "lineage": "Rio de Janeiro's own funk lineage from the 1990s favela bailes onward, codified by DJ Marlboro's Volume series, then the tamborzão beat built by DJ Luciano Oliveira circa 1998 from sampled atabaque, timbal and repique hits, and carried by Cidinho e Doca, MC Cidinho, Bonde do Tigrão and the proibidão MCs — 125-135 BPM in a syncopated non-four-on-floor pattern, minimal or absent harmony, call-and-response chanted refrains, and lyrics reporting favela life and command territory, recorded fast and pressed straight to CD or sound-system playback.",
